{
  "evaluation": "All three correctly treat the genetic proxy for vitamin D as on-question and identify the cohort-versus-Mendelian-randomization contrast as design_or_bias. C is strongest because it explicitly flags that Study A's quoted sentence does not support its harm label, while retaining the classification warranted by the supplied headline findings. A also acknowledges the unstated direction and gives a grounded comparison. B is slightly weaker because it describes the GWAS datasets as large even though their sample size is not reported. All three reasonably identify population and outcome-measure differences.",
  "ranking": ["C", "A", "B"]
}
